"""A source-attributed working glossary; physical terms are not moral labels."""
SOURCES={
 'waves':'https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/13-2-wave-properties-speed-amplitude-frequency-and-period',
 'interference':'https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/14-4-sound-interference-and-resonance',
 'force':'https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/15-6-forced-oscillations',
 'plate':'https://amhistory.si.edu/science/chladni.htm',
 'history':'https://cymascope.com/cymatics-history/',
 'postulate':'https://cymascope.com/four-postulated-laws-of-cymatics/',
 'fft':'https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/tutorial/fft.html',
 'signal':'https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/tutorial/signal.html',
 'schumann':'https://areas.geofisica.unam.mx/schumann/',
 'rules':''}

# Definitions are concise paraphrases or explicit app contracts, never copied articles.
# Checks describe this app's operational tests, not claims that a sensor is connected.
ROWS=[
 ('Cymatics','Visible patterns produced when vibration acts on matter.','Record the medium, geometry, excitation and observed pattern.','history','unclassified'),
 ('Hans Jenny’s cymatics','Jenny’s investigations documented vibration patterns in different materials.','Keep the cited experiment separate from later spiritual interpretations.','history','unclassified'),
 ('CymaScope','An instrument developed to visualize sound-related patterns using a vibrating medium.','Identify the actual instrument and capture method before calling an image a measurement.','history','unclassified'),
 ('Cymatic spiritual interpretation','A meaning attributed to a vibration pattern by a teaching or observer.','Store the speaker, context and interpretation; do not substitute it for a physical measurement.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Postulated cymatic laws','Proposed generalizations presented as postulates by their authors.','Retain the word postulated and distinguish a proposal from independent validation.','postulate','unclassified'),
 ('Chladni figure','A particle pattern revealing low-motion regions of a vibrating plate.','Compare recorded patterns while holding plate conditions fixed.','plate','unclassified'),
 ('Nodal line','A line of little or no motion in a vibration mode.','Locate particle accumulation in a documented plate experiment.','plate','unclassified'),
 ('Plate geometry','The size and shape of a plate influence its vibration patterns.','Record dimensions; do not assign one universal pattern to a frequency.','plate','unclassified'),
 ('Plate thickness','A physical property affecting a plate’s vibration and resulting tone.','Compare measured thickness with the observed modes.','plate','unclassified'),
 ('Mechanical coupling','Connected objects can transmit vibrations between them.','Identify the physical connection and compare both recorded responses.','plate','unclassified'),
 ('Frequency','The number of cycles occurring per second.','Measure cycle rate; express it in hertz.','waves','unclassified'),
 ('Period','The time taken for one complete cycle.','For a periodic signal, compare period with one divided by frequency.','waves','unclassified'),
 ('Amplitude','Maximum displacement from an equilibrium value.','State the quantity, units and reference; digital amplitude is not pressure.','waves','unclassified'),
 ('Wavelength','Spatial separation between equivalent points of successive cycles.','Requires a spatial measurement or known wave speed.','waves','unclassified'),
 ('Wave speed','The rate at which a wave disturbance propagates.','Relate speed to frequency and wavelength in the specified medium.','waves','unclassified'),
 ('Resonance','Enhanced driven response near a system’s natural frequency.','Sweep frequency while recording amplitude and keeping drive conditions controlled.','force','unclassified'),
 ('Natural frequency','A system’s characteristic oscillation frequency under its physical conditions.','Identify the system; it is not determined by a moral label.','force','unclassified'),
 ('Damping','Loss of oscillation energy over time.','Measure the decay of a recorded oscillation.','force','unclassified'),
 ('Driving frequency','The frequency of the force exciting an oscillator.','Distinguish the imposed drive from the observed response.','force','unclassified'),
 ('Constructive interference','Overlapping waves combine to increase displacement at a location and time.','Compare phase and combined amplitude; increased amplitude is not automatically beneficial.','interference','unclassified'),
 ('Destructive interference','Overlapping waves partly or fully cancel displacement.','Compare combined amplitude; cancellation is not synonymous with damage or evil.','interference','unclassified'),
 ('Beat frequency','Amplitude variation arising from nearby frequencies interfering.','Compare measured modulation with the absolute frequency difference.','interference','unclassified'),
 ('Fundamental','The lowest frequency in a harmonic vibration series.','Identify it from the particular source, not from the strongest peak alone.','interference','unclassified'),
 ('Harmonic','A component at an integer multiple of a fundamental frequency.','Compare measured peak ratios with the candidate fundamental.','interference','unclassified'),
 ('Overtone','A resonant frequency above a fundamental.','Identify the physical system; an overtone need not be an integer harmonic.','interference','unclassified'),
 ('Discrete Fourier transform','A decomposition of sampled data into discrete frequency components.','Use the actual sampling rate and sample count.','fft','unclassified'),
 ('FFT','An efficient method for computing a discrete Fourier transform.','Validate known test signals before interpreting unknown recordings.','fft','unclassified'),
 ('Frequency bin','One frequency coordinate in a discrete spectrum.','This inspector’s bin spacing equals sampling rate divided by window samples.','fft','unclassified'),
 ('Real FFT','A Fourier transform specialized for real-valued samples.','Retain the nonredundant nonnegative-frequency spectrum.','fft','unclassified'),
 ('Inverse transform','Reconstruction of samples from frequency-domain coefficients.','Check reconstruction error against the original samples.','fft','unclassified'),
 ('Nyquist frequency','Half the sampling rate; the highest distinct frequency represented without alias ambiguity.','Limit selectable bands to half the file’s sampling rate.','fft','unclassified'),
 ('Window function','A weighting applied to a finite segment before spectral analysis.','The inspector reports a Hann-window spectrum.','signal','unclassified'),
 ('Spectral leakage','Spreading of spectral energy caused by finite observation windows.','Compare window length and weighting before interpreting nearby peaks.','signal','unclassified'),
 ('Power spectrum','Frequency-domain representation of signal power under a specified scaling.','Use consistent normalization when comparing recordings.','signal','unclassified'),
 ('Band power fraction','The fraction of analyzed spectral power within a selected frequency range.','Sum measured bins in that range and divide by total analyzed power.','signal','unclassified'),
 ('Spectrogram','A sequence of spectra showing frequency content over time.','Read time, frequency and intensity scales separately.','signal','unclassified'),
 ('Schumann resonances','ELF electromagnetic resonances of the Earth–ionosphere cavity.','A suitable electric or magnetic receiver is required for direct readings.','schumann','unclassified'),
 ('Schumann fundamental variation','The measured first resonance peak can vary with environmental conditions.','Retain station, timestamp and measured frequency; do not assume every reading is 7.83 Hz.','schumann','unclassified'),
 ('Station-specific observation','A reading obtained at a particular receiver location.','Show station identity and do not describe it as an exact global instantaneous waveform.','schumann','unclassified'),
 ('Digital full scale','The maximum amplitude represented by the audio sample format.','Flag samples near 0.999 normalized magnitude; this alone does not prove clipping.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('RMS amplitude','Square root of mean squared sample amplitude.','Compute from decoded PCM samples; report digital units.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Spectral centroid','Power-weighted mean frequency in this implementation.','Compute sum(frequency × power) divided by total power.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Waveform isolation','Reconstruction retaining only selected frequency bins.','Report the band, window, attenuation and possible edge ringing.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Emotive interpretation','An interpretation of emotional tone based on supplied content and context.','Label it inferred; waveform energy does not establish intention or personal feelings.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Moral lesson','A source-grounded interpretation of a teaching’s implications for conduct.','Cite supporting dialogue or observations and retain alternative readings.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Scene observation','An account of a specific action or event in a video.','Record timestamp, observer and whether frames were actually inspected.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Caption evidence','Words retrieved from a caption track.','Preserve source, language and whether captions were automatic.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Measured impact','A change in a defined outcome compared with a stated baseline.','Record before/after values; do not claim causation from concurrent activity.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Unresolved classification','A case lacking enough evidence for a supplied good/evil criterion.','Keep the bit unchanged and mark its label unknown.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Good-preserving bit rule','A supplied good label preserves either binary value.','Verify both 0→0 and 1→1 for virtue pass and fail.','rules','good'),
 ('Evil-flipping bit rule','A supplied evil label flips either binary value.','Verify 0→1 and 1→0 for virtue pass and fail; a label is not inferred from the bit.','rules','evil'),
 ('Protective care','The framework’s commitment to protecting vulnerable life and supporting repair.','Look for documented need, appropriate consent, protection and outcomes.','rules','good'),
 ('Restorative action','Action intended to repair damage while respecting those affected.','Record what was damaged, the proposed repair, and evidence of delivery.','rules','good'),
 ('China Doll care','The user’s spiritual metaphor of careful restoration and protection of fragile life.','Connect the named scene to attributed observations; do not claim infinite protection is measured.','rules','good'),
 ('Eco-floor elevation','Improving access to defined essentials without lowering another protected floor.','Compare documented availability before and after, using explicit units.','rules','good'),
 ('Rightful earnings protection','Preserving legitimate earnings in the user’s resource framework.','Require an explicit protected amount before proposing surplus allocation.','rules','good'),
 ('Beneficial top preservation','Protecting resources that support legitimate and beneficial activity.','Separate protected resources from eligible surplus.','rules','good'),
 ('Resource conservation','A proposal must not allocate more stock than is available.','Check exact quantities and protected reserves.','rules','good'),
 ('Truthful uncertainty','Clearly stating where facts, definitions or causal evidence are missing.','Retain pending states rather than fabricate a positive result.','rules','good'),
 ('Redemptive transition','A supported movement toward repair and changed conduct.','Distinguish intention, proposed action, partial progress and evidenced outcome.','rules','good'),
 ('Respectful community support','Support based on the priorities and agency of the people concerned.','Record locally documented needs and participation; do not infer need from identity alone.','rules','good'),
 ('Harmful action','Conduct producing a documented adverse effect under a defined criterion.','Describe the effect, evidence, affected interests and uncertainty.','rules','evil'),
 ('Extractive deprivation','Taking resources in a way that lowers a protected essential floor.','Compare the proposed transfer with protected reserves and recipient need.','rules','evil'),
 ('Coercion','Pressure that defeats meaningful choice in the relevant context.','Require contextual evidence; a model label is not a legal finding.','rules','evil'),
 ('Deception','A materially misleading representation under a specified evidential standard.','Compare the representation with supported facts and retain uncertainty about intent.','rules','evil'),
 ('Predatory exploitation','Taking advantage of vulnerability under the framework’s protection criteria.','Document the conduct and harm; do not infer it from wealth or group membership.','rules','evil'),
 ('Forced positive convergence','Changing inputs or labels merely to make an evaluation report success.','Compare original facts with transformed facts and flag unsupported substitutions.','rules','evil'),
 ('False accusation','An unsupported assertion presented as an established finding of wrongdoing.','Separate observations, allegations, interpretations and human adjudication.','rules','evil'),
 ('Basic-floor deprivation','Withholding defined essentials as punishment or a scoring consequence.','The framework disallows automatic deprivation based on model classifications.','rules','evil'),
 ('Bit provenance','The relationship between a bit, its supplied meaning and the operation applied.','Log index, input, label, evidence, rule and output.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Trajectory sweep','Repeated application of a specified transition rule.','Show intermediate states; repeated evil flips have period two.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Cast-back receipt','Evidence that transformed bytes entered the application’s shared queue.','Check queue acceptance, processed bytes and hashes; queued does not mean processed.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Inverse verification','A check that reversing a permitted transform restores its input.','Compare recovered bytes exactly with original bytes.','rules','unclassified'),
 ('Definition provenance','The source and context behind a reusable meaning.','Keep URL, retrieval time, evidence excerpt and interpretation status.','rules','unclassified')]


def glossary():
    return [{'id':'precise-'+str(i),'term':term,'definition':meaning,'operational_test':check,'orientation':orientation,
             'url':SOURCES[source],'title':'Cymatics / signal reference' if source!='rules' else 'Observatory working criterion',
             'basis':'curated source paraphrase' if source!='rules' else 'Operational interpretation of user goals and implemented contracts',
             'status':'reference definition; not an automatic classification of people','targets':[]} for i,(term,meaning,check,source,orientation) in enumerate(ROWS)]
